vars:pre-request {
  locationsUrl: http://localhost:3001
  propertiesUrl: http://localhost:3002
}

docs {
  # m324 Real Estate

  Demo requests for the two microservices.

  | Service      | Local                   | Production                              |
  | ------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
  | `locations`  | http://localhost:3001   | https://m324-locations.onrender.com     |
  | `properties` | http://localhost:3002   | https://m324-properties.onrender.com    |

  Without an environment the requests go to localhost. Pick **Production** in
  the top right to target Render instead, then run the requests in order.
  "Create locality" stores the new id and postal code in runtime variables,
  which the later requests reuse.

  Production runs on Render's free tier: the first request after a while can
  take up to a minute while the instance wakes up.
}
